  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1030 PM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nThursday through Monday:\n\nThursday expect a trough aloft and departing low with an \nincoming high to keep weather in play into Thursday primarily \nbringing breezy north to northeast winds across the region. \nGiven cooler conditions behind the front with still very warm \nlake waters surface to 850mb temperature differences will \nballoon to 15-20 degrees. With some very slight onshore wind \npotential some lake effect rain showers are possible in far\nsoutheast WI, right along the lake but will otherwise remain dry\nfor most of southern WI and even most of southeast WI. Thursday\nnight into Friday these conditions will remain but more\nnortherly winds will keep chance over the lake with high\npressure keeping southern WI dry and likely mostly clear.\nHowever, if we were to manage some lake effect over the area\nThursday night into Friday a few flakes would be possible.\n\nConditions this weekend continue to look dry as high pressure\nremains overhead and likely even strengthens through the weekend\nand lingers through early next week. \n\nKuroski",
